    "background_story": "Carson was a rising star in the world of finance, known for his exceptional analytical skills and bold investment strategies. As a portfolio manager at a prestigious firm, he had a knack for identifying undervalued stocks and predicting market trends. However, Carson's true passion was distance running. He would often use the early morning hours before work to log miles and clear his mind. His training paid off when he qualified for the Boston Marathon, a lifelong goal. As the big day approached, Carson's friends and colleagues noticed a peculiar correlation between his running performance and the market's behavior. Whenever he had a strong run-up in his training, the stocks he managed would inexplicably surge. Carson's colleagues began to jokingly refer to his marathon training as a 'market indicator,' and he became known as the 'running bull' of Wall Street.",
